From 0d13a7950244837415cbf38daadfd11753ff8bd2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 16:09:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] joan-common: Add the AOSP IMS stack

VoLTE, Wi-Fi calling, SMS over IMS, video calling, RTT and emergency
calls through AOSP's IMS stack. The V30's modem was built without
Qualcomm's IMS core, so IMS has to run on the AP: SIP, IPsec and call
media in ImsStack and ImsMedia, the Wi-Fi calling tunnel in IWLAN, and
the choice between LTE and Wi-Fi in QNS.

ImsStack is not in Android 15. It and ImsMedia come from Android 17
(android-17.0.0_r1) with the backport patches from
https://github.com/ShapeShifter499/joan-volte-lineage (aosp-ims/),
synced by the local manifest in that repository's upstream/aosp-ims/.
IWLAN and QNS are the tree's own.

- Build ImsStack, ImsMediaService, Iwlan and QualifiedNetworksService,
  and declare android.hardware.telephony.ims.
- Make ImsStack the device's ImsService for MMTEL and RCS capability
  exchange; allow VoLTE, Wi-Fi calling, video calling and RTT on the
  device; bind AOSP IWLAN and QNS in place of vendor.qti.iwlan, which
  needs the modem IMS this modem does not have.
- Carrier config: VoLTE and Wi-Fi calling for every SIM, with the VoLTE
  toggle kept usable, and ePDG addresses for AT&T, Verizon and T-Mobile
  MVNOs. Generated by aosp-ims/tools/make-carrier-config.py; that
  repository's upstream/aosp-ims/apply-patches.sh can add the per-carrier
  IMS config LineageOS converts from Pixel carrier settings.
- Default runtime permissions: microphone and camera for ImsMedia and
  ImsStack, phone state and location for ImsStack, IWLAN and QNS.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SByt7CZfKR6U4r1VS86tHS
